    "matrix collected via serialized GPU queues (night_queue{3,4,5,6}.sh; logs/ per-cell stdout). Process contention policy: one GPU job at a time after the 30B Insufficient-Memory cascade of the first night queue.",
    "Session: openfox-e9e19426 night experiment 2026-10-27/28. bench-repo rev 3cadaaf (working tree adds lanes/, logs/, night_queue*.sh, tools/assemble_lane_matrix.py uncommitted).",
    "Versions pinned: python lane .venv-mlx (uv) mlx 0.32.4 / mlx-lm 0.32.2; Swift mlx-swift 19601207e9a0de51e03ee6ec0c3c5f3784275075 (0.32.3) + mlx-swift-lm 3b339ad6e3b3f44c8121ecff5131c7fd55e075e6; C lane links Swift's own Cmlx.o (Release, same bytes as the L1 app's dylib) -> C==Swift core by construction. Rust initially used mlx-sys 0.6.0 vendored mlx-c (core v0.32.2, patch skew, 62/64-token parity logged in FAILURES LF-11); after the review it binds the SAME 0.32.3 mlx.h and links the same lanes/swift/.build/out/Products/Release/Cmlx.o object (build.rs) -> L3/L4/L5 == L1 engine binary-wise. C/Rust S1-era pre-fix rows kept under results/raw history only.",
    "Metallib provenance matters: the C host with the Python wheel's mlx.metallib ran lm_head dequant+matmul ~4x slower (0.935 vs 0.256 ms/op A/B probe lanes/c/gpu_probe2.c); fix was symlinking lanes/c/mlx.metallib -> the SPM default.metallib from the Swift build. All C/OBJC numbers below are on the SPM metallib.",
    "Native lane numbers are step-count-sensitive: live Metal buffers grow ~2MB/step (dense) in hand-rolled loops until iogpu rsrc_limit 499000 is hit (~550 steps MoE). Cells with decode_steps<768 are short-salvage runs, faster per-step than their long-run average (crashed 768-step attempts recorded in FAILURES.md). mlx_clear_cache every 50 steps does NOT rescue.",
    "Prefill coverage (review C1 fix): L0/L0m/L1/L3/L4/L5 carry prompt_tokens==32/512/2048 cells; L5 (ObjC) is the same qwen3_decode.c rehosted via -x objective-c, rebuilt with the prefill arm. C/Rust/L0m measure prefill AFTER the decode session in identical order (native numbers pessimistic: per-step allocator pressure); L1 reports best-of-4 ttfb over chat-template-calibrated prompts with promptTokenCount verified exact per row.",
    "L2 FoundationModels: FM session wraps the mlx model; completions are short (session policy) and include prompt overhead; t/s not comparable to raw-loop lanes \u2014 recorded separately per FM honesty rule.",
    "Review fixes 7-9 (2026-10-28): kind derived from model id (a3b/moe -> qwen3_moe, 1.7b/4b -> qwen3_dense, else \"unknown\") when the raw row omits model_kind; prefill cells carry unit=ms (median/mean are total prefill ms, throughput stays in derived.prefill_tps); unknown stats are null instead of fabricated 0/768 (iters now derived from run token counts or per_step_ms length when decode_steps is absent).",
    "Host-environment drift is real: same binary+model varied ~2x across the night (Swift 1.7B 182-355 t/s) with load/thermal state. Ranking cells therefore use SAME-SESSION paired A/B (queue11 logs, results/raw/*_q11_*.json \u2014 8 paired rows copied out of /tmp/ post-review so they survive reboot): 1.7B S1=348.3 vs L0m=305.7 (+14%), 4B S1=179.5 vs L0m=159.7 (+11%), reproduced to 0.4% in round B. Single-row t/s from different time windows are not directly comparable."
